## Context

In `slides/manuscript/main.md` figures are included as `![Figure N](path)`
followed by a separate italic caption paragraph. Pandoc's implicit_figures
turns the alt text into a LaTeX `\caption{Figure N}`, which the `figure`
counter prefixes again: the PDF shows "Figure 6: Figure 6", "Figure 7:
Figure 7". Spotted on Figure 6 and Figure 7 (ticket 0446 review); the fix is
the caption *style*, global — not a per-figure patch.

Author decision (2026-06-06, 0446 arbitration): separate ticket, out of the
0446 figure-rework PR. Note: 0446 made Figure 7 an *inline* image (trailing
`\ ` after the image) inside its landscape page, which suppresses the
implicit figure there; the italic-paragraph caption is the visible caption.
That is one candidate convention for the whole document.

## Options to arbitrate

1. Inline-image convention everywhere (`![](path){...}\` + italic caption
   paragraph): kills the duplicated caption, loses LaTeX float/caption
   machinery (acceptable: main.md already hand-numbers its captions).
2. Real pandoc captions (`![Real caption text](path)`): drop the italic
   paragraphs, let pandoc number figures; requires renumber-proofing the
   inline "Figure N" cross-references.
3. `link_attributes` + `{#fig:id}` with pandoc-crossref: heavier toolchain
   change; probably overkill for an arXiv preprint.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One convention chosen and applied to every figure in main.md
- [ ] No "Figure N: Figure N" duplication anywhere in the built PDF
- [ ] Inline "Figure N" references still resolve to the right figures
- [ ] `make manuscript` green; visual check of every figure page

## Related

- 0446 (matrix figure rework — where the defect was confirmed live)
- 0435 (arXiv finalization — consumes the fixed build)
